---
import LandingLayout from '../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';

const rawBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = rawBase.endsWith('/') ? rawBase : `${rawBase}/`;
---

<LandingLayout
  title="Evaluate Local GCP Development Costs — LocalCloud"
  description="A methodology for comparing local-emulation and real-GCP development costs without unsupported savings claims or unlicensed team-use assumptions."
>
  <section class="site-section site-section--hero">
    <div class="container"><div class="max-w-[52rem] reveal">
      <span class="site-eyebrow"><span class="site-eyebrow__pulse"></span>Cost evaluation</span>
      <h1 class="mt-4">Measure your own local-development cost trade-off</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)] sm:text-xl">LocalCloud does not publish a maintained savings benchmark. Use your own billing exports, workload profile, hardware cost, engineering time, and production-validation requirements.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a href={`${base}docs/licensing/`} class="site-button site-button--primary">Review licensing first</a><a href={`${base}compatibility/`} class="site-button site-button--secondary">Review compatibility</a></div>
    </div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-section site-section--tight"><div class="container"><aside class="callout callout--warning"><div class="callout__body"><p class="callout__title">For-profit use requires a Commercial License</p><div class="callout__content"><p>A for-profit company must obtain a separate Commercial License before using LocalCloud for cost reduction, internal tools, development workflows, or team CI. Community use remains free for eligible individual developers, students, and nonprofit organizations. Review the <a href={`${base}docs/licensing/`}>Licensing reference</a>.</p></div></div></aside></div></section>

  <section class="site-section"><div class="container">
    <div class="site-section-heading reveal"><span class="site-kicker">Method</span><h2>Build a reproducible comparison</h2><p>Record assumptions instead of copying generalized percentages or dollar ranges.</p></div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3 stagger">
      <article class="site-panel p-5"><h3>1. Establish the baseline</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">Use dated billing exports to isolate developer, test, staging, and CI usage by service. Exclude unrelated production spend.</p></article>
      <article class="site-panel p-5"><h3>2. Define the workflow</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">List exact SDK versions, services, operations, data volume, test frequency, retention, and required fidelity.</p></article>
      <article class="site-panel p-5"><h3>3. Check evidence</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">Map each operation to the compatibility contract. Release-unverified and unsupported behavior needs a different test path.</p></article>
      <article class="site-panel p-5"><h3>4. Include local costs</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">Account for compute, storage, Docker infrastructure, maintenance, developer time, and the cost of failed fidelity assumptions.</p></article>
      <article class="site-panel p-5"><h3>5. Keep production validation</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">Budget for guarded tests against real Google Cloud for IAM, quotas, regional behavior, managed integrations, performance, and release confidence.</p></article>
      <article class="site-panel p-5"><h3>6. Measure, do not extrapolate</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">Run a time-boxed evaluation and compare observed bills and cycle time. Publish the date, hardware, workload, and exclusions with any result.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="site-section"><div class="container"><div class="site-panel p-6 reveal"><h2>Estimate checklist</h2><ul class="site-list mt-5"><li>Dated billing data with project and service filters.</li><li>The LocalCloud image or CLI release being considered.</li><li>Service support levels and known gaps.</li><li>Local infrastructure and maintenance cost.</li><li>Real-GCP release-validation scope.</li><li>Governing license review for the intended user and purpose.</li></ul></div></div></section>
</LandingLayout>
